  "title": "Answer: observation is a quantum-to-classical exchange",
  "statements": [
    {
      "id": "fd8dc1b4-38c1-4dae-9af9-394b11452374",
      "text": "The occurrence of an outcome is a quantum-to-classical information exchange, and conditioning on it a classical-to-quantum one. An outside observer gets only the epistemic, mixed state and at best a single complementary side of an experience.",
